## Configure Slurm on the Compute Nodes

Point each compute node's `slurmd` at the head node (configless mode) and enable
it. The setting is written before the service is enabled, so a stateful node
that applies this after boot starts `slurmd` with it already in place.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure Slurm on the compute nodes -->
```bash
# Register the Slurm server with the computes (configless mode)
{{ compute_run("echo SLURMD_OPTIONS=--conf-server ${sms_ip} > /etc/sysconfig/slurmd") }}
{{ compute_service_enable("slurmd.service") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{%- if is_xcat_stateless %}

The image carries no munge key, so at boot `munge` and `slurmd` start before the
synclist delivers it. Add a short script to the synclist that xCAT runs on the
node after every sync, to start them once the key is in place:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Start munge and slurmd once the synced key is in place -->
```bash
cat > ${xcat_synclist_dir}/ohpc-postsync << 'EOF'
#!/bin/sh
systemctl is-active -q munge.service  || systemctl restart munge.service
systemctl is-active -q slurmd.service || systemctl restart slurmd.service
EOF
chmod 755 ${xcat_synclist_dir}/ohpc-postsync
echo "${xcat_synclist_dir}/ohpc-postsync -> /usr/local/sbin/ohpc-postsync" \
    >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "EXECUTEALWAYS:" >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "${xcat_synclist_dir}/ohpc-postsync" >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
{%- endif %}
